# Boilerplate

Read and follow [`CLAUDE.md`](../../CLAUDE.md) for all work in this repo.

That file is the contract: folder layout, git and branch rules, docs ownership, security, testing,
and where feature state lives. Do not invent parallel rules here.

## Quick pointers

- Feature plan in `docs/plans/` + row in `docs/project.md` before code
- Open questions → `docs/open-questions.md`; defects → `docs/defects.md`
- Prefer project skills (`/book:self-review`, `/book:commit`, `/book:ship`, the docs skills) over ad hoc process
- The Book's skills come from the book plugin (`/book:<name>`); a project's own, if any, go under `.claude/skills/`.
- Each folder with its own `CLAUDE.md` has a scoped rule beside this one that points at it
- Never commit to a protected branch directly — open a pull request
- The specification wins every requirements conflict
